    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0363" n="231" xml:id="pg231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860h.00/7–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 197 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Yugoslavia </hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shantz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d197-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d197-f2"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-07T14:00:00+02:00">July 7, 1945—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>247. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p> Šubašić expressed hope that Big Three meeting will make a public reference to
                        this<anchor n="3" xml:id="d197-f3"/> and remind Yugo Govt that
                    [Tito-Šubašić] agreement<anchor n="4" xml:id="d197-f4"/> must be carried out.
                    …</p>
                <p> Stevenson and I believe such action desirable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shantz</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d197-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d197-f1-content">
                <p>The gist of this message was included in telegram No. 11 of July 10 from Grew to
                    Byrnes (file No. 740.00119 Potsdam/7–1045).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d197-f2" n="2" xml:id="d197-f2-content">
                <p>For the full text of this message, see <ref target="#d553">document No.
                    553</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d197-f3" n="3" xml:id="d197-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d553">document No. 553</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d197-f4" n="4" xml:id="d197-f4-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1945Malta#pg_251">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, The Conferences at Malta and
                        Yalta, 1945, pp. 251</ref>–<ref target="frus1945Malta#pg_254">254</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
